<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shalmaneser V</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">reigned 727–722 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shalmaneser V was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a> from 727 to 722 BCE, son and successor of Tiglath-Pileser III. When King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoshea">Hoshea of Israel</a> stopped paying tribute, he besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samaria">Samaria</a>, which fell around 722 BCE, ending the northern kingdom. He died or was overthrown at about that time, and his successor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-ii">Sargon II</a> claimed the conquest and deported much of Israel's population.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shalmaneser-v.jpg" alt="Shalmaneser V" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Osama Shukir Muhammed Amin FRCP(Glasg) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shalmaneser_V_crown_prince.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
